      "card_ids": ["C212", "C223", "C210"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus intravenous exposure data exist for the query.",
    "No query-specific permeability, efflux, or intestinal metabolism measurements exist; L5 records are for other molecules.",
    "Structural analogy to flupenthixol, trazodone, imidafenacin, and fluphenazine is qualitative.",
    "P-gp substrate status of the query is not experimentally established."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is a basic phenothiazine-like amine with a sulfonyl and piperidine carboxamide side chain. L1 contexts (flupenthixol 30-70%, trazodone 63-91%, imidafenacin 57.8%) support F >= 20%. L4 C180 supports near-complete GI absorption for a methylsulfonyl-piperidine analog. L5 adds only mechanistic gut-wall efflux evidence: C212 shows fluphenazine, the closest phenothiazine, is a P-gp substrate with efflux ratio 2.30, but this is not a direct F outcome and is offset by L5 examples of P-gp substrates with adequate absorption (C223, C210). No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20%. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

